==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|fancy|-able|text=+|tree=1}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|UK|informal}} [[worthy|Worthy]] or [[likely]] to be [[fancy#Verb|fancied]]; [[sexually]] [[attractive]].
#: {{syn|en|crushworthy}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|author=w:Eden Phillpotts|chapter=Mother’s Misfortune|title=The Torch and Other Tales|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/files/15737/15737-h/15737-h.htm|page=105|publisher=Macmillan|location=New York
|passage={{...}} I wondered where the poor soul had seen a less '''fanciable''' maiden than herself in our village, or any other.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=w:Bernardine Evaristo|title=w:Girl, Woman, Other|location=London|publisher=Hamish Hamilton|chapter=Yazz
|passage=she’s only been on one date at uni, which involved sitting at a bar with a male specimen she’d thought was an interesting person, who was obviously swiping his phone to see if someone more '''fanciable''' was in the vicinity before making his pathetic excuses about having to do revision}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} Able to be [[fancy#Verb|fancied]] ([[imagine]]d or [[suppose]]d).
#: {{syn|en|imaginable}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1936|title=Code of Georgia Annotated|publisher=Harrison Company|page=155|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=pcRJAQAAIAAJ&q=%22fanciable%22&dq=%22fanciable%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjKzZLCh4T4AhXDqY4IHTFPCdQQ6AF6BAgaEAI
|passage=doubt reasonably and fairly entertained as opposed to vague or '''fanciable''' doubt}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1948|title=Standard Federal Tax Reporter|publisher=Commerce Clearing House|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=w_AKAQAAMAAJ&q=%22fanciable%22&dq=%22fanciable%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjKzZLCh4T4AhXDqY4IHTFPCdQQ6AF6BAgYEAI
|passage={{...}} the factual basis for such a contention is more '''fanciable''' than real.}}

